<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">French First Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1792 CE – 1804 CE · capital Paris</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The revolutionary republic that executed a king, fought most of Europe, passed through the Terror and the Directory, and ended in Napoleon's empire.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the storming of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuileries-palace">Tuileries</a> in August 1792, a newly elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-convention">National Convention</a> abolished the monarchy of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-france">Kingdom of France</a> on 21 September 1792 and proclaimed the Republic. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xvi">Louis XVI</a> was tried and executed in January 1793, while French armies fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Facing war and revolt, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-convention">Convention</a> gave power to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/committee-of-public-safety">Committee of Public Safety</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximilien-robespierre">Robespierre</a>; the Terror executed thousands before his fall in July 1794. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-directory">Directory</a> governed from 1795 amid corruption and coups. The Republic introduced the metric system, abolished feudal dues and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> in 1794, and conquered <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-belgium">Belgium</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland">Rhineland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon Bonaparte</a> seized power in the coup of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coup-of-18-brumaire">18 Brumaire</a> in 1799 and governed as First <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">Consul</a>, restoring order through the Concordat of 1801 and the Civil Code. In May 1804 the Republic was transformed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/french-empire">First French Empire</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/french-first-republic.jpg" alt="French First Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown Vector: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_France.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1792 CE – 1804 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Paris</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Maximilien Robespierre, Paul Barras, Napoleon Bonaparte</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a>, <a href="/countries/belgium">Belgium</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>First Republic, National Convention France, French Directory</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1798&amp;focus=french-first-republic" aria-label="French First Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4734 472 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where French First Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5054 728L5054 728M5054 728L5811 1337M5054 728L5054 728M5054 728L5121 874M5054 728L5116 700M5054 728L5171 761M5054 728L5159 768M5054 728L5160 738M5054 728L5140 827M5054 728L5178 884M5054 728L5229 916M5054 728L5141 706M5054 728L5127 676M5054 728L5135 683M5054 728L5099 670M5054 728L5097 634M5054 728L5133 661M5054 728L5153 701M5054 728L5162 673M5054 728L5170 716M5054 728L5161 717M5054 728L5145 668M5054 728L5141 673M5054 728L5139 672M5054 728L5158 667M5054 728L5194 714M5054 728L5192 705M5054 728L518